	<version>0.0.1-SNAPSHOT</version>
	<packaging>pom</packaging>

	<name>OSGi® Specification Project</name>
	<description>The OSGi® Specification
		Project is an open source initiative to
		create new, and evolve existing, software specifications,
		implementations of those specifications, and Technology Compatibility
		Kits (TCKs) for those specifications that enable development,
		deployment, and management of embedded, server-side and cloud-native
		applications. The OSGi Specification Project is based on Specifications,
		Reference Implementations and Compliance Tests of the former OSGi
		Alliance and uses those materials as the baseline for creating new
		specifications, implementations and TCKs, or revising existing OSGi
		Alliance specifications, reference implementations and compliance tests.
		The OSGi Specification Project software specifications enable
		development, deployment and management of embedded, server-side, and
		cloud-native applications by using software modularity to vastly improve
		the evolution, maintainability, and interoperability of applications and
		infrastructure.
	</description>

	<organization>
